ode_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":15,"created_at":"2025-09-26T07:07:33Z","updated_at":"2026-02-07T12:35:41Z","closed_at":"2025-11-27T10:51:54Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110920","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110920","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110920.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110920.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"This adds an inline quick load button to the script editor, like the color picker. This works for all ((triple-) single-quoted, (triple-) double-quoted) strings that start with `res://` or `uid://`. It's different from what was suggested in the discussion (only have it on `load`/`preload` calls), but I think this way it works for more use-cases like a custom load method.\r\n\r\nIt has four modes:\r\n* Off\r\n* Only uid - only creates `uid://` paths\r\n* Only res - only creates `res://` paths\r\n* Preserve - respects whatever it is currently\r\n\r\n[Screencast_20250925_235258.webm](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/37c3832d-ef3f-4b2d-8bf9-15986773c065)\r\n\r\nThis also adds inline hints for UID paths:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"617\" height=\"290\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ff7c29b5-c3d6-4daf-8e32-492902fbe9b8\" />\r\n\r\nWhile this isn't exactly like the chip mockup, I think it's more readable since you can see both the `res://` path and the original UID path.\r\n\r\nI refactored the inline object handlers from just being for the color picker to merge results from multiple sources, so maybe adding new inline objects will be easier in the future. I used a RegEx to locate the strings for easier development, I'm not sure if it's fine but I'm not sure it's easily possible to do it the same way the color picker does it.\r\n\r\nResolves godotengine/godot-proposals/discussions/13192","closed_by":{"login":"sockeye-d","id":106356149,"node_id":"U_kgDOBlbdtQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106356149?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d","html_url":"https://github.com/sockeye-d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110920/reactions","total_count":52,"+1":19,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":18,"confused":0,"heart":10,"rocket":3,"eyes":2},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110920/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}